From: =?UTF-8?q?Ant=C3=B3nio=20Sarmento?= <Keyaku@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 17:36:03 +0100
Subject: SystemUI: survive a Bluetooth profile losing its active device

`onActiveDeviceChanged` passes null when a profile no longer has an active device, which is exactly what happens when a wired headset takes over audio from Bluetooth. The debug log dereferenced it unguarded and took SystemUI down with an NPE. Unreachable on this device until wired-jack detection started working.

Changes:
- Null-guard the active-device address in the debug log, printing "none" when the profile has no active device.

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I522f5d5a06317481d17f83dbddc55f9ac2480277
---
 .../systemui/statusbar/policy/BluetoothControllerImpl.java   | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/policy/BluetoothControllerImpl.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/policy/BluetoothControllerImpl.java
index eeadf4a4..d58341b4 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/policy/BluetoothControllerImpl.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/policy/BluetoothControllerImpl.java
@@ -384,7 +384,10 @@ public class BluetoothControllerImpl implements BluetoothController, BluetoothCa
     @Override
     public void onActiveDeviceChanged(CachedBluetoothDevice activeDevice, int bluetoothProfile) {
         if (DEBUG) {
-            Log.d(TAG, "ActiveDeviceChanged=" + activeDevice.getAddress()
+            // activeDevice is null when the profile loses its active device,
+            // which a wired headset taking over audio does.
+            Log.d(TAG, "ActiveDeviceChanged="
+                    + (activeDevice == null ? "none" : activeDevice.getAddress())
                     + " profileId=" + bluetoothProfile);
         }
         updateActive();
